-- expect: rejected
-- A machine whose continuation is a closure instead of a frame: a step answers `done b`, or
-- `rec(a)` with the rest of the computation as a function of the answer. The type of what a
-- step answers occurs in its own continuation's result, under `U`, which the checker refuses. So
-- the continuations of `rec` are defunctionalised: frames, data (`rec.bc`). The same refusal
-- blocks `mu X. !(X => i32)`, the self-applicable type a knot-tying `fix` would need.

type Out = mu X. i32 + (i32 * U (i32 -o F X))

main -> i32 = 0
